<!-- BAND 5: COMPARISON — CMP, FLUTTER, REACT NATIVE -->
<section id="compare" class="prose-section prose-section-alt">
  <div class="site-container">
    <div class="prose-header-center reveal-on-scroll">
      <p class="prose-eyebrow">Framework Comparison</p>
      <h2 class="prose-h2">Skip the <span class="prose-gradient">either/or</span> trade-off</h2>
      <p class="prose-lead">
        Every other cross-platform stack forces a bet between canvas-drawn lookalikes and a JavaScript bridge.
        Osprey Native spans both worlds in one ahead-of-time binary.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="spectrum-grid reveal-on-scroll" aria-label="Cross-platform rendering spectrum">
      <div class="spectrum-card">
        <span class="spectrum-kicker">Canvas-Only Stack</span>
        <strong>Flutter &amp; Compose Multiplatform</strong>
        <p>Draws its own copies of widgets onto Skia or Impeller. Native platform controls require interop wrappers; CMP runs desktop on the JVM.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="spectrum-card">
        <span class="spectrum-kicker">JS Runtime Stack</span>
        <strong>React Native</strong>
        <p>Renders real mobile platform views, but ships a JavaScript engine (Hermes) and leaves custom GPU canvases to native modules.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="spectrum-card spectrum-card-winner">
        <span class="spectrum-kicker">&#10003; Both Worlds &middot; Zero JS &middot; Zero JVM</span>
        <strong>Osprey Native</strong>
        <p>Choose genuine SwiftUI, WinUI, and Android views <strong>or</strong> FerroUI's GPU canvas &mdash; one AOT codebase, signals, and enforced accessibility.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div tabindex="0" role="region" aria-labelledby="compare-caption" class="table-wrapper reveal-on-scroll">
      <table class="compare-table">
        <caption id="compare-caption">Architectural comparison: Osprey Native vs. Compose Multiplatform (CMP), Flutter, and React Native</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Capability</th>
            <th scope="col" class="col-osprey">Osprey Native</th>
            <th scope="col">Compose Multiplatform (CMP)</th>
            <th scope="col">Flutter</th>
            <th scope="col">React Native</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Rendering model</th>
            <td class="col-osprey"><span class="cell-chip">&#10003; Both Modes</span><br>Real native controls (SwiftUI, WinUI, Android) <strong>OR</strong> FerroUI / GPUI GPU canvas</td>
            <td>Skia canvas for shared UI (native views require platform interop wrappers)</td>
            <td>Impeller / Skia canvas only (framework-drawn widget copies)</td>
            <td>Native platform views only (custom GPU scenes need native modules)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Runtime &amp; compilation</th>
            <td class="col-osprey"><span class="cell-chip">&#10003; AOT Native</span><br>LLVM machine code everywhere + WebAssembly on web; no JS engine, no JVM</td>
            <td>Kotlin/Native on iOS, JVM on desktop &amp; Android, Wasm/JS on web</td>
            <td>Dart AOT on mobile &amp; desktop, JS/Wasm on web</td>
            <td>JavaScript engine (Hermes) + JSI / native bridge</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Reactivity</th>
            <td class="col-osprey"><span class="cell-chip">&#10003; Compiler Signals</span><br>Built-in <code>Signal&lt;T&gt;</code> &amp; keyed regions from the ground up</td>
            <td>Compose Snapshot state + compiler recomposition</td>
            <td>Widget tree rebuilds + third-party state packages</td>
            <td>React hooks + virtual DOM reconciliation</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">Language &amp; syntax</th>
            <td class="col-osprey"><span class="cell-chip">&#10003; Multi-Flavor</span><br>Default Osprey, ML, Python, TypeScript flavors (Dart coming soon; Kotlin considered)</td>
            <td>Kotlin only</td>
            <td>Dart only</td>
            <td>JavaScript / TypeScript only</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
